@startuml DockerSandboxExperiment
'  covers: internal/sbx/sbx.go, cmd/proveo/main.go (sandbox.Run/sandbox.Spec),
'          e2e/sbx_test.go
' EXPERIMENT → ADOPTED (subscription harnesses). claudecode + cursor run on the
' sbx backend when available (internal/sbx; auto with docker+egress fallback);
' the egress layer is reserved for open-source harnesses (opencode, cecli).
' Cursor's egress hole remains the owning question for full adoption.
'
' Docker Sandboxes research (2026-07, sbx v0.35.0 — "generally stable", pre-GA):
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/                     — landing (microVM per workspace)
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/architecture/        — hypervisor boundary; own kernel + engine + net
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/security/isolation/  — deny-by-default egress; cred injection
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/security/defaults/   — locked-down defaults
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/usage/               — sbx run/exec/cp/ports/policy/secret
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/kits/      — Kit spec.yaml (declarative config)
'   https://www.docker.com/blog/docker-sandboxes-run-agents-in-yolo-mode-safely/
'
' proveo bespoke stack this would collapse (source of the "TODAY" boxes):
'   internal/egress/{plan,exec,stage}.go  — networks/sidecars/teardown (firewall = 3 nets + Squid + MITM)
'   internal/egressproxy/*                 — TLS-MITM proxy + per-session CA + NDJSON flows
'   internal/broker/broker.go              — credential inject / strip
'   internal/egresspolicy/*                — DLP secret scanner (regex + base64/hex + entropy + sink denylist)
'   internal/dind/dind.go + defs/sidecars/dind    — privileged docker:dind sidecar (RETIRED, _spec/_plans/retire-dind.puml)
'   internal/runner/runner.go + defs/base/proveo-harden — cap-drop/no-new-priv/pids-limit + setuid strip
'   packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh         — arbitrary run-as-uid + HOME/passwd synth
'   internal/egress/exec.go + cmd/proveo/clean.go — teardown + leaked-artifact reaper
!includeurl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/refs/heads/main/proveo.iuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 12
skinparam ranksep 60

title Experiment — proveo on Docker Sandboxes (""sbx"", free tier)\nCursor egress hole is the owning question; microVM may also collapse the bespoke stack

package "TODAY — proveo bespoke isolation\n~2,800 LOC Go · 10 pkgs · 5 sidecars · 3 nets · per-session MITM CA" as today #FBECEC {
  component "egress planner\ninternal/egress\nnets · sidecars · DNS blackhole · teardown" as p_egress
  component "MITM proxy + per-session CA\ninternal/egressproxy" as p_mitm
  component "credential broker\ninternal/broker\ninject on-provider · strip off-provider" as p_broker
  component "DLP secret scanner\ninternal/egresspolicy\nregex · base64/hex · entropy · sink denylist" as p_dlp
  component "privileged DinD sidecar\ninternal/dind + docker:dind — DELETED" as p_dind
  component "hardening\ninternal/runner + defs/base/proveo-harden\ncap-drop · no-new-priv · setuid strip" as p_harden
  component "run-as-uid + HOME/passwd synth\npackages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh" as p_uid
  component "ephemeral lifecycle + leak reaper\nexec.go teardown + clean.go" as p_life
}

package "WITH sbx — Docker Sandboxes microVM\nhypervisor boundary · standalone sbx CLI · v0.35 (pre-GA)" as sbx #EBF3EC {
  component "sbx run «agent» «workspace»\none command; one microVM per workspace" as s_run
  component "Kit spec.yaml\nnetwork.allowedDomains / deniedDomains\ncredentials · environment  (deny wins)" as s_kit
  component "host-side egress proxy\ndeny-by-default allowlist · DNS-gated\nraw TCP/UDP/ICMP + private IPs blocked" as s_egress
  component "host-side credential injection\nvalues never enter the VM · sbx secret set" as s_cred
  component "per-sandbox Docker Engine\nno host socket · no privilege" as s_engine
  component "microVM\nown kernel + rootfs · non-root + sudo\nsbx rm ⇒ ephemeral (VM + images + volumes)" as s_vm
}

p_egress ..> s_egress : collapses to a declarative allowlist
p_mitm   ..> s_egress : no MITM CA to mint / mount / trust
p_broker ..> s_cred   : same principle — inject, never expose
p_dlp    ..> s_kit    : deny-by-default ⇒ no non-allowlisted sink
p_dind   ..> s_engine : killed the privileged sidecar — done
p_harden ..> s_vm     : hypervisor is the boundary
p_uid    ..> s_vm     : sandbox-managed user
p_life   ..> s_vm     : sbx rm deletes the VM

note right of sbx #E7F0FF
  **Advantages / simplifications**
  • one ""sbx run"" replaces the ""run.Do""/""execWithEgress"" orchestration
  • a declarative allowlist replaces the ""plan.go"" multi-net + MITM topology
  • host-side credential injection already matches proveo's broker (convergent design)
  • a private Docker Engine per sandbox REMOVED privileged DinD + its consent gating (shipped)
  • deletes ~5 sidecar images and the per-session CA mint/mount/trust machinery
  • the hypervisor boundary makes the in-guest hardening no longer load-bearing
end note

note top of today #E7F0FF
  **Owning question: Cursor's egress hole (free-tier sbx only)**
  cursor pins TLS to "".cursor.sh"" / "".cursor.com"" → proveo declares
  ""egress:[open] credentials:[forward]"" — no MITM, no Squid. Cursor's
  Landlock sandbox needs unprivileged userns and fails with EPERM inside
  the cap-dropped container, so the entrypoint keeps ""--sandbox disabled"".
  Result: container FS/process boundary only; network unconstrained.

  Free path this experiment targets (no AI Governance subscription):
  • host-side deny-by-default proxy + local ""sbx policy allow"" for
    "".cursor.sh"" / "".cursor.com"" (Kit ""allowedDomains"")
  • credentials stay **forward** — header injection still wants TLS
    intercept Cursor will not allow
  Explicit non-goal: Docker AI Governance (org-central policy, audit
  logs, sales licenses). Local ""sbx policy"" is enough for the Cursor gap.
end note

note left of sbx #FFF3F0
  **Also unlocked (secondary): claudecode container work — DONE**
  claudecode never took DinD: it was broker-only and a privileged escape
  hatch (""docker run -v /:/host --privileged""). The per-sandbox Docker
  Engine inside the microVM (no host socket, no privilege) unlocked
  container work without that downgrade, and then replaced the sidecar
  outright (_spec/_plans/retire-dind.puml). claudecode still cares most
  about the DLP content-scan gap below.
end note

note bottom of sbx #F3F0FB
  **No docker engine substitutes for this.** proveo names the engine behind the
  docker CLI (OrbStack, Docker Desktop, Colima, Rancher Desktop, Podman, Lima),
  but every one of them shares a single Linux kernel — the engine is a naming
  concern, not an alternative backend. See
  ""_spec/internal/engine/container-engine\.puml"".
end note

note bottom of today #FFF6E5
  **Caveats — why this stays an experiment**
  • platform-gated: macOS Apple-Silicon · Linux + KVM · Win11 Hyper-V
    (proveo runs anywhere Docker does)
  • ""sbx"" v0.35 — "generally stable" but no formal GA yet
  • microVM RAM overhead (default 50% of host, cap 32 GiB)
  • AI Governance (org-enforced policy + audit logs) is a **separate
    paid subscription** — optional; **not required** for the Cursor
    free-tier local-policy experiment
  • DLP **content** scan (base64/entropy on payloads to *allowed* hosts) has **no
    sandbox equivalent** — the proxy allowlists domains + injects headers, it is
    NOT a TLS-terminating body inspector → a capability gap, not just a simplification
    (hurts claudecode more than cursor, which never had MITM DLP)
  • ""sbx"" ships its own agent templates ⇒ adoption reframes proveo as
    **Kits/templates on sbx** (re-expressing the harness images, the run capability
    picker, the LSP/browser layers), not a ""docker run"" wrapper
end note

' ── MEASURED, sbx v0.39.0 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Everything below this line was measured on this host against v0.39.0, not read
' from the docs. It is recorded because each item cost a wrong diagnosis first.

package "MEASURED — what sbx v0.39.0 actually does\nrun on macOS Apple Silicon, images built locally" as m #FFF6E5 {
  component "**template load ≠ what runs**\n""sbx create"" re-BAKES the loaded template\nand rewrites the store's IMAGE ID column" as m_bake
  component "**a baked template can go bad**\nevery create fails until the image is\nloaded again; ""sbx diagnose"" stays 12/12" as m_rot
  component "**no docker daemon inside**\nno socket · no DOCKER_HOST\n""Cannot connect to the Docker daemon""" as m_nodocker
  component "**built-in agents cannot be shadowed**\nclaude · codex · copilot · cursor · docker-agent\ndroid · gemini · kiro · opencode · shell" as m_agents
  component "**a workspace must be a DIRECTORY**\n""workspace path exists but is not a directory""" as m_ws
  component "**pullPolicy is not a Kit field**\nrejected under ""sandbox:"" and at top level" as m_pull
}

m_bake   ARROW_MAIN  m_rot      : the bake is what rots
m_bake   ARROW_ERROR m_nodocker : and what drops the client

note bottom of m_bake #E7F0FF
  **Identity must be recorded, not read back.** Loading puts the host image's ID
  under the reference; ONE ""sbx create"" later the same row names a different
  image — measured, ""2ca281d785dc"" → ""5fcb2266417f"" for proveo/claudecode:latest.

  So ""HasTemplate"" cannot compare against that column: after the first run it
  mismatches forever and re-loads a multi-GB tar on EVERY launch. It compares a
  **receipt** proveo writes at load time instead, which still reloads a genuine
  rebuild and ignores a bake. The staleness the ID check was added for is real —
  a repo-tag-only match once served a pre-rebuild image with no ""/app"" at all —
  so presence alone is not enough either.
end note

note bottom of m_rot #FFF3F0
  **The reload that was removed was also a repair.** While proveo re-loaded the
  template on every run, a bad bake was overwritten before anything could run on
  it. Making the load conditional is right — it is the slowest step in a sandbox
  run by a wide margin — but it exposed the rot: cursor reached a state where
  EVERY ""sbx create"" failed with "failed to run sandbox container", including
  argv that had succeeded minutes earlier, with ""sbx diagnose"" reporting 12/12
  healthy. A single ""sbx template load"" repaired it.

  So the repair is now explicit and narrow: one retry on a freshly loaded
  template, taken ONLY when ""sbx.Exists"" says no sandbox by that name was
  created. That is the line between a sandbox that never started and an agent
  that ran and exited non-zero — retrying the latter would run the agent twice.
  It cannot be read off sbx's output: sbx prints that ERROR on **stdout**, and
  stdout is the agent's terminal, so wrapping it to sniff for the text would
  leave sbx writing to something that is not an ""*os\.File"" — exactly what its
  own PTY checks look for.
end note

note right of m_nodocker #FFF3F0
  **SUPERSEDED — the daemon is a LABEL away, and the label is now set.** This box
  recorded a real measurement: neither def reached a daemon, no
  ""/var/run/docker.sock"", no ""DOCKER_HOST"", ""docker version"" answering "Cannot
  connect to the Docker daemon". The cause was not the absence of a feature but a
  missing image label — sbx starts a per-sandbox daemon only for an image carrying
  ""com.docker.sandboxes.start-docker"" (_spec/internal/sbx/sbx-kit-contract.puml).
  With it: Server 29.7.2 inside a proveo sandbox. So ""docker: sbx"" now means the
  sandbox SUPPLIES docker, behind the boundary — which is what let ""docker: dind""
  be retired rather than kept for harnesses that need one.

  **The docker CLIENT is deliberately NOT asserted on, in either direction.**
  Its survival is an sbx implementation detail and it is not uniform: from images
  that both install ""/usr/local/bin/docker"", cursor's sandbox keeps it and
  claudecode's does not — the claude-flavoured bake replaces it with
  ""sbx-clipboard"", ""wl-paste"", ""xclip"" and ""xdg-open"". Asserting either way
  would encode that detail as a proveo contract and break on the next release.

  This was diagnosed WRONG first: the missing binary read as "sbx strips the
  docker client", and the inverse assertion written from it would have failed
  cursor, whose sandbox has one. What is stable is that nothing reaches a daemon.
end note

note right of m_agents #E7F0FF
  A ""kind: sandbox"" Kit DECLARES an agent, and sbx refuses to let a declaration
  shadow a built-in — ""agent "cursor" is already registered (built-in agents
  cannot be overridden by a kit)"". Two of proveo's four defs are named after
  built-ins, so the Kit's agent is namespaced ""proveo-<target>"".

  The name is one value, not two: sbx also refuses ""agent name X does not match
  agent kit name Y"", so ""Kit.Name"" and the positional move together.

  Namespacing beats checking against today's list, because the list grows: a
  collision test would pass until sbx shipped an agent named like one of ours.
  The failure it avoids is silent — cursor's runs died ~12s in, session gone
  before the shell, nothing captured, which read as a timeout for as long as the
  error stayed unread.
end note

note right of m_ws #E7F0FF
  sbx mounts each positional at its own HOST path and refuses anything that is
  not a directory. Two kinds of proveo bind are therefore dropped on this backend:
  a bind with a container-side target (proveo home at ""/proveo-home"", the gh
  config under it), and a bind of a FILE — the project ""\.env"", and the
  ""/dev/null"" masks the credential policy layers over it.

  Consequence worth stating plainly: **a project ""\.env"" does not reach an sbx
  sandbox.** On the brokered tiers it was being masked away regardless, and the
  credentials it would have carried are declared in the Kit instead.

  Home is passed as a workspace with ""HOME"" pointed at its host path, since
  ""/proveo-home"" cannot be expressed; ""PROVEO_WORKDIR"" tells the harness where
  the workspace actually landed, there being no ""-w"" on an sbx run.
end note

note bottom of m_pull #FFF6E5
  ""pull_policy"" (always · missing · never) exists inside sbx, but it is not a
  Kit field: the validator rejects ""pullPolicy"" both under ""sandbox:"" and at the
  document root. So a Kit cannot pin "never pull" — ""sbx create"" always runs its
  own PREPARE IMAGE step over the reference it was handed.

  Left as a finding rather than a workaround. The local-per-user hand-off is
  still the right shape (each operator has their own docker login and their own
  sbx config), and the receipt above is what keeps proveo honest about which
  image it handed over.
end note

note as m_open #FBECEC
  **OPEN — cursor stops right after its shell appears.** With the workspace,
  agent-name and template fixes in, cursor creates a sandbox, prints
  ""cursor@<sandbox>:<workspace>$"" and is then stopped —
  ""ERROR: sandbox "<name>" was stopped"", proveo exits 1. claudecode completes the
  same flow. Not yet diagnosed; ""sbx"" has an "auto-stopped runtime after last
  session disconnected" path that is the first place to look.

  ""TestEveryHarnessGetsTheDockerAccessItPromises"" reports it by name rather than
  as a timeout, which is the point of that probe.
end note


@enduml
